[#:seon.task{:name "a-status-observation-costs-half-a-gigabyte"
             :kind :function
             :intent "problems costs 150 ms and 502 MB per call (deferred-agents 108 ms / 363 MB over 44 agents x deferred-triggers, failed-tests 37 ms / 102 MB), and runtime_status observes twice (discovery health, then the observation). Derive status once and make deferred-agents follow changed agents. 2026-09-27 (152ceb62c): deferred-agents asks only messaged agents (114 -> 3 ms at 123 agents), open-faults reuses the attached resolution (12 -> 0.1 ms); problems 204-279 -> 92-98 ms warm on default. Open: failed-tests is ~75 ms, all in `seon.test.runner/latest-results` over 1,288 test symbols, of which admitted-members' history check over every involved run's members is 53 ms; it grows with recorded executions (8,712 members), not with the 144 failing now."
             :must-read #{seon.problems/deferred-agents seon.problems/problems seon.turn/deferred-triggers seon.problems/open-faults}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/perf-profile-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/perf-audit-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "ai-prose-returns-printed-text-not-data"
             :kind :function
             :intent "ai-prose (src/seon/problems.clj:604) is the `:seon.render/ai` face of the problems value but returns the value printer's text (its contract is :string): it builds the family -> steering-lines map and calls `seon.render.value/render-ai` itself. A render returns data and the value printer prints it, so the face should return that lines map (with its requery offer) and leave printing to the edge. Until then seon.problems-test asserts the face's output only as text (includes the model id / stale Var) and six-hundred-failed-tests-render-within-the-profile-bound is a declared golden (test-data-assertions lane, 2026-09-28)."
             :must-read #{seon.problems/ai-prose seon.render.value/render-ai}
             :evidence #{"test/seon/problems_test.clj"}} #:seon.task{:name "an-error-many-agents-hit-is-a-seon-defect"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Errors delivered to agents are never recorded, so health misses a reader or tool defect that many agents hit (chain run 2: `Unable to resolve symbol: </invoke>` three times, 21 agent errors, 0 platform errors). `seon.problems/problems` derives `:seon.problems/agent-error-signatures` from each agent's branch evaluation errors (`:seon.cluster.eval/error`): one pattern with its distinct agents, occurrences, values and latest example, once `:seon.config.error/agent-error-agents` agents hit it, as the finding schema `:seon.problems/agent-error`. Reads undecoded through `seon.db/undecoded-datoms`."
             :must-read #{seon.problems/problems seon.problems/open-faults seon.db/branch-database seon.db/undecoded-datoms}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/bench/e0-e1.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "problems-prose-carries-no-date-or-file-line"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Also give `seon.problems/deferred-agents` a complete `:malli/schema` (it has none; merge acceptance refuses a merge that carries an uncontracted function, as landing of 15b7e49ebafb showed): its input is the database value (`:seon.db/database-value`) and its output the vector of deferred-agent entries it returns; read its body and callers, and name existing schema keys rather than inventing new ones. AGENTS.md: no dates, measurements, history or `file:line` in source. Four functions of seon.problems carry an ISO date or a `<name>.clj:<n>` citation in their docstring: `seon.problems/error-signatures`, `seon.problems/deferred-agents`, `seon.problems/failed-tests`, `seon.problems/ai-prose` (confirmed on default 450dca226: `:seon.fn/doc` of those four, no other function of the namespace). Correct: redefine each with `defn` in the namespace `seon.problems` (read the whole source first with `(my.program/source 'seon.problems/failed-tests)`), its docstring keeping its meaning and dropping the date or the citation (the dated audit belongs in Git or the owning spec); the body, contract and metadata stay as they are. Done when `seon.source-census-test/problems-prose-carries-no-date-or-file-line` answers []: it reads `:seon.fn/doc` of every function of seon.problems from the branch database (custody, not files), so your redefinition is what it checks. Run it at your REPL with `(clojure.test/run-test-var #'seon.source-census-test/problems-prose-carries-no-date-or-file-line)` after the four `defn`s. A comment is not a program fact and the census does not read it; the four findings are docstrings. Its limit, the six census tests that still read files, is `seon.census/a-census-reads-the-program-its-branch-holds`."
             :must-read #{seon.problems/error-signatures seon.problems/deferred-agents seon.problems/failed-tests seon.problems/ai-prose seon.contracts/task}
             :evidence #{"test/seon/source_census_test.clj"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "two-outcomes-at-one-key-are-a-nondeterministic-test"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(hybrid-test-results R12) Two outcomes at one key are a problem of the test. New family `:seon.problems/nondeterministic-tests` in `seon.problems/families` (schema in `resources/seon/schemas/seon.problems.edn`), derived inside `seon.problems/failed-tests`' existing read from the members at one key with different outcomes, each entry carrying both run ids; `seon.test.runner/results-at` answers the newest, so nothing waits and nothing reruns. A test reading cluster data it did not write surfaces here (owner: not keyed). Red proof: new `seon.problems-test/two-outcomes-at-one-key-are-a-nondeterministic-test`: two fixture runs of one test at one key, the second with `:seon.test/rerun?` and its body reading a value the fixture changes between runs, one green and one red, give one entry with both run ids (HEAD: no family). Cost: under 10 ms added to `failed-tests`. Files: `src/seon/problems.clj`, `src/seon/test/runner.clj`, `resources/seon/schemas/seon.problems.edn`, `test/seon/problems_test.clj`"
             :must-read #{seon.problems/failed-tests seon.problems/families seon.test.runner/latest-results}
             :needs #{[:seon.task/sym seon.turn/a-read-only-request-re-runs-the-branchs-reaching-tests]}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/hybrid-test-results.md"}}]
